From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:21:26 +0900
Subject: Mobile file dialog: save to a typed full path

The save button made the URL as the folder shown + "/" + the typed text: a full path typed into
the field (/home/kevinzhow/Pictures/drawing.kra) became file:///home/kevinzhow/Pictures//home/
kevinzhow/Pictures/drawing.kra, a folder that does not exist; the application then failed to save
or, with a Qt application, kept waiting (docs/103). A typed full path or file URL is now used as
given, a name still goes into the folder shown. Each part of the path is percent-encoded, so a
name with # or ? is not cut at it. An empty name no longer saves to the folder itself, and Enter in
the field saves as the button does.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a plain bug; check upstream master first]
X-Rungic-Tests: tools/tests/test_mobile_file_dialog.py (the save row from this hunk, offscreen Qt Quick); the whole dialog by hand on the phone, docs/103
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/103
---
 src/kirigami-filepicker/declarative/FilePicker.qml | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kirigami-filepicker/declarative/FilePicker.qml b/src/kirigami-filepicker/declarative/FilePicker.qml
index e7d213e..17acedb 100644
--- a/src/kirigami-filepicker/declarative/FilePicker.qml
+++ b/src/kirigami-filepicker/declarative/FilePicker.qml
@@ -99,12 +99,23 @@ Kirigami.ScrollablePage {
                 Layout.fillWidth: true
                 id: fileNameField
                 placeholderText: i18n("File name")
+                onAccepted: saveButton.clicked()
             }
             Controls.ToolButton {
+                id: saveButton
                 Layout.fillHeight: true
                 icon.name: "dialog-ok-apply"
+                enabled: fileNameField.text.length > 0
                 onClicked: {
-                    root.fileUrls = [dirModel.folder + "/" + fileNameField.text]
+                    const typed = fileNameField.text
+                    if (typed.length === 0)
+                        return
+                    // Each part of the path percent-encoded: a name with # or ? stays a name.
+                    const encoded = typed.split("/").map(encodeURIComponent).join("/")
+                    // A full path (or a file URL) is used as given; a name goes into the folder shown.
+                    root.fileUrls = [typed.startsWith("file:") ? typed
+                                     : typed.startsWith("/") ? "file://" + encoded
+                                     : dirModel.folder + "/" + encoded]
                     root.accepted(root.fileUrls)
                 }
             }
